      "headline": "Sofia Coppola borrowed three Radio Dept. songs",
      "snippet": "The Radio Dept.'s debut album, Lesser Matters, earned rave reviews and a 'universal acclaim' score on Metacritic, even though it sold little outside Sweden. NME ranked it the ninth best album of 2004. The attention reached film producer Sofia Coppola, who used three of the band's songs in her film Marie Antoinette.",
